        "procedure": "H4Lr (0.100 g, 0.311 mmol) and triethylamine (0.063 g, 0.622 mmol) in absolute ethanol (40 mL) were mixed with dysprosium(III) nitrate hexahydrate (0.142 g, 0.311 mmol) in absolute ethanol (25 mL). The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 h, filtered, and left to slowly evaporate. After a few days, single crystals of 2·2H2O formed. The same complex was obtained at a 1.25:1 Dy:ligand ratio with yield increased to 28%. Peroxide ligands are attributed to fixation/reduction of atmospheric O2; repeating under Ar did not give this peroxo cluster.",
